This is a major design flaw/feature of the game. I can understand the
reasoning, but nobody REALLY goes out and kills everybody named Tom
he meets just because somebody named Tom robbed him once. It also
penalizes micro users more, because they'll ALWAYS run into their
own bones files, rather than somebody else's. I dislike this feature
intensely (in case you hadn't guessed), and my solution has been to
cheat, by deleting all bones files. Sure, you miss out on ghost piles,
but after 3 or 4 times dying because of an accident 12 games back,
it gets annoying. Well, such is life. Or, as the case may be, death.

